#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the logic slice — the test-DSL
# twin of the SHACL shapes in slices/core/logic/shapes.ttl ("this instance must
# validate, that counter-example must be rejected"). The harness
# (crates/slicetest run_conformance_cell) validates logic/module.ttl + the one
# bound gmeow:exampleFile against logic/shapes.ttl and compares finding codes.
#
# MESSAGE→CODE shift: the original shapes assert specific sh:message strings;
# these cells pin the constraint-component CODE (shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>,
# from gmeow_validate::findings::finding_from_shacl). The code form COLLAPSES
# distinct sh:message strings that share a constraint component — e.g. two
# different missing-property violations both report shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent,
# indistinguishable by code alone. Because each counter-example is a SEPARATE
# fixture isolating ONE violation, the (fixture, code) pair still pins the
# specific constraint faithfully.
#
# CODE VERIFICATION: expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent"
# matches the code produced by gmeow_validate::findings::finding_from_shacl for
# sh:minCount violations, confirmed against the unit tests in
# crates/validate/src/findings.rs (MinCountConstraintComponent test, line ~263).
#
# The CONFORMING fixture lives under tests/conformance-fixtures/ (NOT examples/)
# and the two counter-examples under tests/counter-examples/, so the global
# `make validate` gate never loads them as data; they are validated SLICE-SCOPED
# only (module + slice shapes), intentional and mirroring the concepts slice
# exclusion rationale.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed FormalizationCandidate -------------------------
ex:ecCandidateWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/candidate-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies all eight universal carrier properties (candidateSourceHash, candidateExtractionProvenance, candidateScope, candidateContract, candidateCategory, candidateLifecycle, candidateProjectionBehavior, candidateSemanticRisk), each single-valued and pointing to the correct type, so it satisfies logic:FormalizationCandidateShape and validates with no findings." .

# --- Violating: FormalizationCandidate missing candidateSourceHash -----------
ex:ecCandidateMissingSourceHash a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/candidate-missing-sourcehash.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits logic:candidateSourceHash (sh:minCount 1 on logic:FormalizationCandidateShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# --- Violating: FormalizationCandidate missing candidateCategory -------------
ex:ecCandidateMissingCategory a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/candidate-missing-category.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits logic:candidateCategory (sh:minCount 1 on logic:FormalizationCandidateShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Canonical process model conformance cells
# =========================================================================== #

# --- Conforming: a well-formed Plan ------------------------------------------
ex:ecPlanWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/plan-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture supplies exactly one logic:planGoal (a gmeow:Goal) and exactly one logic:planSuccessMode (logic:WeakPlanSuccess), satisfying logic:PlanShape with no findings." .

# --- Violating: Plan missing planSuccessMode ---------------------------------
ex:ecPlanMissingSuccessMode a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/plan-missing-successmode.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits logic:planSuccessMode (sh:minCount 1 on logic:PlanShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed GoalEvaluation --------------------------------
ex:ecGoalEvaluationWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/goalevaluation-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture carries exactly one value of each of the four factored axes (logic:satisfactionStatus, logic:feasibilityStatus, logic:lifecycleStatus, logic:goalEvaluationStatus), one logic:evaluatesGoal, and a single optional logic:satisfactionDegree, satisfying logic:GoalEvaluationShape with no findings." .

# --- Violating: GoalEvaluation missing feasibilityStatus ---------------------
ex:ecGoalEvaluationMissingFeasibility a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/goalevaluation-missing-feasibility.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits logic:feasibilityStatus, one of the four required factored axes (sh:minCount 1 on logic:GoalEvaluationShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# --- Conforming: a well-formed ActionSchema ----------------------------------
ex:ecActionSchemaWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/actionschema-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture carries the two required facets (logic:precondition, logic:capability) plus optional single-valued logic:effect / logic:observation and two multi-valued logic:nondeterministicOutcome values, satisfying logic:ActionSchemaShape with no findings." .

# --- Violating: ActionSchema missing capability ------------------------------
ex:ecActionSchemaMissingCapability a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/actionschema-missing-capability.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example omits logic:capability, one of the two required facets (sh:minCount 1 on logic:ActionSchemaShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# --- Conforming: an MCP-action schema under the governance profile -----------
ex:ecMcpActionWellformed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/mcp-action-wellformed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture's ex:mcpActionWellformed (typed logic:McpActionSchema, the marker logic:McpActionPolicyShape targets) declares the three required governance facets — logic:capability, logic:precondition, logic:compensation (rollback) — satisfying the profile (and, as a subtype, logic:ActionSchemaShape) with no findings." .

# --- Violating: MCP-action schema missing compensation (rollback) ------------
ex:ecMcpActionMissingCompensation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/mcp-action-missing-compensation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example's ex:mcpActionMissingCompensation (typed logic:McpActionSchema) omits logic:compensation (sh:minCount 1 on logic:McpActionPolicyShape — an MCP tool that mutates state with no rollback), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding." .

# --- Conforming: satisfiedBy backed by a vantage-scoped GoalEvaluation -------
ex:ecSatisfiedByBacked a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/satisfiedby-backed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The fixture's conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy(goal, situation) edge is backed by a logic:GoalEvaluation under a vantage (logic:evaluationEvaluator) with evaluatesGoal = goal, evaluatedAgainst = situation, satisfactionStatus = logic:Satisfied, goalEvaluationStatus = logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, so logic:SatisfiedByBackedByEvaluationShape's sh:sparql constraint does NOT fire and the backing evaluation also satisfies logic:GoalEvaluationShape — no findings." .

# --- Violating: satisfiedBy with no backing GoalEvaluation -------------------
ex:ecSatisfiedByUnbacked a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/satisfiedby-unbacked.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example asserts a conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy(goal, situation) edge with NO backing logic:GoalEvaluation under any vantage, so the vantage-scoped dual-authority sh:sparql constraint on logic:SatisfiedByBackedByEvaluationShape fires and validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. The check is never a global verdict: it fires only because no vantage backs the edge at all (Principle 9)." .

# --- Conforming: a STRONG-CYCLIC plan is valid canonically (DAG profile case) -
ex:ecDagStrongCyclicPlan a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/dag-strong-cyclic-plan.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A strong-cyclic logic:Plan (logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess) with a retry LOOP in its control flow is valid CANONICALLY: it carries exactly one logic:planGoal and one logic:planSuccessMode, satisfying logic:PlanShape with no findings — a loop is legitimate canonical structure, not a well-formedness defect. This case checks that canonical validity. The loop only places the plan OUTSIDE the certified acyclic fragment: the plan reaches its flow graph through logic:planFlowEdge and runs logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract, so under the DAG-workflow profile (logic:DagWorkflowResource) the SAME plan resolves to `unsupported` with the offending cycle members named by logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently truncated. That produced verdict is exercised end-to-end — the teleology evaluator emits a logic:ReasoningResult carrying logic:EvaluationUnsupported and the logic:dagCycleWitness, pinned by the conformance case conformance/logic/cases/teleology/strong-cyclic-plan, and the same acyclicity authority is unit-tested in the shared certifier (crates/logic dag_profile::strong_cyclic_plan_vs_its_acyclic_projection): the cyclic edge set certifies as a Cycle (unsupported; the witness names the back-edge), and the acyclic projection that drops the back-edge certifies as Certified (complete-for-fragment)." .
